  "summary_en": "Virginia statute authorizing personal delivery devices on sidewalks, crosswalks and low-speed roadways, setting operating requirements (10 mph limit, identification, brakes), pedestrian rights, hazardous materials compliance, $100,000 liability insurance, and criminal liability for misuse.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Devices may operate on sidewalks, crosswalks, and roads with speed limit of 25 mph or less; localities cannot prohibit them.",
   "Devices must obey traffic signals, not block rights-of-way, stay under 10 mph on sidewalks, carry unique ID and operator identification, and have brakes.",
   "Devices on sidewalks have pedestrian rights and responsibilities.",
   "Operators must carry at least $100,000 general liability insurance.",
   "Persons using devices for criminal activity are criminally liable."
  ],
